<urn:atm:triage:finding/ATM-QA-S3-004>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "ATM-QA-S3-004" ;
  triage:title "recover_stale_owner_lock uses 25ms × 3 fixed sleep without documented constraint (host_ownership.rs)" ;
  triage:description "crates/atm-daemon/src/host_ownership.rs — recover_stale_owner_lock() retries with thread::sleep(OWNER_RECOVERY_RETRY_INTERVAL) × 3 = 75ms fixed sleep. plan-phase-S.md §4.1 Anti-Flake Contract prohibits fixed sleeps without documented justification. The OS file-lock APIs provide no release-notification surface, making polling necessary; this constraint is undocumented. Fix: add inline comment at the sleep call documenting (a) this is an error path only, (b) OS lock APIs have no release notification, (c) bounded at 75ms max. TASK-1158 added a comment at a different location; QA-4 confirms the sleep at :119 still has no inline comment. Confirmed STILL_OPEN at 8b17139. (quality-mgr reported as ATM-QA-NEW-002 in S.3 QA-2 report.)" ;
  triage:category "ATM-QA" ;
  triage:severity "important" ;
  triage:triageMode "followup_pass" ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-S" ;
  triage:repeatable false ;
  triage:sweepScope "file" ;
